    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d89">

                <pb facs="0144" n="72" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg72"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 1571/1.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Rockhill to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1906-09-06"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">September 6, 1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 390.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith for
                    the information of the department a clipping from the North China Daily News of
                    August 27, with reference to the Huangpu conservancy.</p>
                <pb facs="0145" n="73" xml:id="pg73"/>
                <p>The article is a valuable one, in that it contains a summary of events up to the
                    present conservancy scheme and shows the manner and condition of the work which
                    is now being undertaken.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. W. Rockhill.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d89-a1.xml" xpointer="d89-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
